g margin 25.5%, +327bps YoY) and robust free cash flow (FCF margin 40.6%, FCF growth +20.4%). ROE is exceptionally high at 62% though ROIC is not computable given the financial-sector balance sheet structure (zero reported debt, negative net debt of $11.2B cash). Shareholder returns are strong via buybacks (7.3% yield) reducing diluted shares by 5.2% YoY, though total shareholder yield (8.7%) is funded disproportionately by buybacks over dividends (1.3% yield).","technical_read":"Price is in a confirmed downtrend on short/medium timeframes (below 20/50-day SMAs, MACD negative) but 50-day remains above 200-day (longer-term uptrend intact), with price just below the 200-day MA itself (-0.2% distance) and 13.7% off 52-week highs. RSI at 29.9 signals oversold conditions, which combined with the 50>200 structure could set up a mean-reversion bounce, though momentum signals are presently bearish.","market_expectation":"The market is pricing AMP for stagnation or decline\u2014an 11x P/E at the 0th percentile of its own 5-year history and a 0.4 PEG\u2014despite observed double-digit revenue and FCF growth, implying investors are either skeptical of growth durability in asset management or are rotating capital away from Financials broadly regardless of company-specific fundamentals.","what_market_misses":["Reality score (61) running well ahead of pricing score (38), a 23-point expectations gap that is unusually wide","Revenue acceleration (+2.3pt QoQ) is not reflected in any valuation re-rating","Margin expansion and FCF growth (+20.4%) suggest operating leverage is strengthening faster than the market is crediting","Aggressive buyback program (7.3% yield) is structurally shrinking the share count, which should compound per-share value if growth sustains"],"catalysts":["Next quarterly earnings report (~90 days after the 2026-08-04 filing) could validate or refute continued revenue acceleration and margin trends","A shift in Financials sector rotation sentiment from current d